==========================================
CLOUD/DEVOPS DAY 02 NOTES — EC2/VPC Concepts + DynamoDB
Date: 24-11-2026
==========================================

WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- LocalStack Community does NOT emulate EC2 (Pro-only) - EC2/VPC covered as theory today
- EC2 instance = a virtual server; AMI = the template/image it's built from; instance type = its size/specs
- VPC = isolated virtual network; subnets split it into public/private zones
- Security Groups are STATEFUL instance-level firewalls (return traffic auto-allowed)
- DynamoDB (NoSQL) IS supported in LocalStack Community - full hands-on done
- DynamoDB table/item roughly maps to a SQL table/row, but schema-less per item

COMMANDS I PRACTICED:
[ ] docker run ... -e SERVICES=s3,iam,dynamodb ...
[ ] awslocal dynamodb create-table ...
[ ] awslocal dynamodb put-item / get-item
[ ] awslocal dynamodb scan
[ ] awslocal dynamodb delete-table

paste your real output here :
$ awslocal dynamodb get-item --table-name Day02Practice --key '{"id": {"S": "item1"}}'
